  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0106 database contains 14 tables that store information about Formula One races, drivers, and constructors. The tables are designed to store the following information:\n1. Circuits: This table contains information about the circuits where races are held, including the circuit's name, location, country, latitude, longitude, and altitude.\n2. Constructor Results: This table contains information about the results of each constructor in a particular race, including the points scored, the status of the constructor (e.g. \"active\", \"inactive\"), and the race ID.\n3. Constructor Standings: This table contains information about the standings of each constructor in a particular race, including the points scored, the position of the constructor, the number of wins, and the race ID.\n4. Constructors: This table contains information about the constructors participating in a particular race, including the constructor's name, nationality, and URL.\n5. Driver Standings: This table contains information about the standings of each driver in a particular race, including the points scored, the position of the driver, the number of wins, and the race ID.\n6. Drivers: This table contains information about the drivers participating in a particular race, including the driver's name, number, code, date of birth, nationality, and URL.\n7. Lap Times: This table contains information about the lap times of each driver in a particular race, including the lap number, position, time, and milliseconds.\n8. Pit Stops: This table contains information about the pit stops of each driver in a particular race, including the stop number, lap number, time, duration, and milliseconds.\n9. Qualifying: This table contains information about the qualifying results of each driver in a particular race, including the position, number, and time.\n10. Races: This table contains information about the races, including the year, round, circuit ID, name, date, time, and URL.\n11. Results: This table contains information about the results of each driver in a particular race, including the position, position text, points, laps, time, milliseconds, and status.\n12. Seasons: This table contains information about the seasons, including the year and URL.\n13. Status: This table contains information about the status of each driver in a particular race, including the status (e.g. \"active\", \"inactive\").\n14. Target: This table contains information about the target of each driver in a particular race, including the win.\nEach table has its own set of columns, with some tables having foreign keys that reference other tables. The primary keys in each table are used to uniquely identify each row, and the foreign keys are used to establish relationships between tables. The database is designed to store and retrieve data in a structured and organized manner, making it easy to analyze and visualize the data.",
  "gold_question": "Ergast F1 Historical Data Web Service\n\n 1) Background / Context\nErgast.com provides a comprehensive database of Formula 1 race data, starting from the 1950 season to the present. It includes detailed information about races, circuits, drivers, constructors, and their performances in various aspects such as lap times, pit stops, and qualifying rounds.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe main objective of Ergast.com is to offer a rich set of historical data for Formula 1 enthusiasts, researchers, and developers through a web service interface. It aims to support data-driven analysis and provide an accessible platform for querying detailed F1 statistics.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Primary Users: Formula 1 analysts, data scientists, researchers, and developers interested in motorsports data.\n- Secondary Users: Formula 1 fans and historians seeking insights into historical race data.\n- Stakeholders: Motorsports organizations, educational institutions, and software developers using the data for applications or research.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Database Access: Users can query detailed information about races, circuits, drivers, constructors, lap times, pit stops, qualifying results, and standings.\n- Race Information: Access data on individual races, including year, round, location, and results.\n- Driver and Constructor Details: Retrieve performance details such as points, standings, and nationality.\n- Performance Metrics: Analyze lap times, pit stops, and qualifying times for drivers and constructors.\n- Historical Trends: Enable statistical analysis and trend identification over multiple seasons spanning several decades.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The database should efficiently handle and process complex queries, accommodating historical data spanning over 70 years.\n- Scalability: Design the system to support a growing dataset with ongoing Formula 1 seasons and increased user queries.\n- Accessibility: Provide a reliable and user-friendly API for accessing the dataset with comprehensive documentation for ease of use.\n- Security: Ensure secure data handling and access controls to protect the integrity and privacy of the dataset.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0106.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0106\nCREATE TABLE `circuits` (\n  `circuit_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(9,6) NOT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(9,6) NOT NULL,\n  `altitude` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`circuit_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `constructor_results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `constructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `points` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `constructor_results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`constructor_id`) REFERENCES `constructors` (`constructor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `constructor_results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `constructor_standings` (\n  `standing_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `constructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `points` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `wins` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`standing_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `constructor_standings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`constructor_id`) REFERENCES `constructors` (`constructor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `constructor_standings_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `constructors` (\n  `constructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`constructor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `driver_standings` (\n  `standing_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `points` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `wins` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`standing_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `driver_standings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `driver_standings_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `drivers` (\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`driver_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `lap_times` (\n  `lap_time_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `lap_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `milliseconds` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`lap_time_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `lap_times_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `lap_times_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pit_stops` (\n  `pit_stop_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stop_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `lap_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `milliseconds` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`pit_stop_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pit_stops_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `pit_stops_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `qualifying` (\n  `qualifying_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`qualifying_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `qualifying_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `qualifying_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `races` (\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `round` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `circuit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`race_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `races_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`circuit_id`) REFERENCES `circuits` (`circuit_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position_text` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `points` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `laps` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `milliseconds` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `seasons` (\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `status` (\n  `status_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`status_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `status_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `status_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `target` (\n  `target_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `race_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `win` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`target_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`driver_id`) REFERENCES `drivers` (`driver_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`race_id`) REFERENCES `races` (`race_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
